<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dumlupınar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1922</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1919-1922">Greco-Turkish War (1919–1922)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dumlupınar was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1919-1922">Greco-Turkish War</a>, fought from 26 to 30 August 1922 in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In the Great Offensive, Turkish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a> broke the Greek lines near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afyonkarahisar">Afyonkarahisar</a> and routed the Greek army at Dumlupınar. The Greek retreat to the coast ended with the Turkish capture of Smyrna on 9 September, and 30 August is celebrated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> as Victory Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dumlupinar.jpg" alt="Battle of Dumlupınar" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Volki16 at Turkish Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kocatepe1922.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
